# Push means GitHub Pages

When the user asks to **push** (including “commit and push”):

1. Commit source to `main` if they asked to commit and there are changes.
2. Push `main` to `origin` if source changed.
3. **Always publish GitHub Pages** from the latest `main`:
   - `$env:GITHUB_PAGES='true'; npm run build`
   - Commit the `dist/` output on the existing `gh-pages` history (fast-forward; do not force-push unless history is unrelated).
   - `git push origin gh-pages`
   - Confirm Pages source is branch `gh-pages`, path `/`.
   - Live URL: https://nonchxlantdev.github.io/bacc-project-main/

Do not treat a `main`-only push as finishing the request. Overlay PDF APIs will not run on static Pages; still publish the UI demo.
